<title>JAPAN: Toyota Motor rises after share purchase plan. [CORRECTED 05:35 GMT]</title>
<headline>Toyota Motor rises after share purchase plan. [CORRECTED 05:35 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>(Corrects headline to read share purchase plan rather than share buy-back)</p>
<p>Shares in Toyota Motor Corp rose in Wednesday trade after the company announced that it would buy 27.8 percent of the shares outstanding in Toyota South Africa Ltd, brokers said. (Corrects to clarify it was a purchase of shares rather than a share buy-back)</p>
<p>At 0138 GMT, the shares were 20 yen higher at 2,700 yen. Turnover was 795,000 shares.  </p>
<p>The shares said it would buy are currently held by Johnnies Industrial Corp (Johnnic) of South Africa and its pension funds.</p>
<p>The total value of the shares is about 10 billion yen, the Japanese car maker said in a statement.</p>
